WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.680
Use this bind off anytime you're ending
your knitting with needles out of work.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.400
You might be working
a tuck lace pattern like this one

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.880
with some needles out of work.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.480
Now, notice my needle arrangement.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:20.880
I have every third needle
in work with two needles out of work.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.680
Let's consider binding
off in this needle arrangement.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.960
I'm using a 'round the gate peg method.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.840
I'll position my working yarn
around the gate peg to the right

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.640
of the stitch that I'm binding off.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.800
I'll pull the yarn through the stitch,
keeping that extra loop

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.120
around the gate peg.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.480
Pull up a loop.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.200
Next, I'll position my latch tool
in the empty space that was created from

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.800
the needle out of work, and I'll just
pull up a loop, creating a chain.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.720
Position the tool in the next space,
keeping keeping the working yarn around

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.520
that gate peg, and chain another loop.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.240
Bind off the next stitch
by putting it on the latch tool,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:15.320
grab the working yarn with the hook
and pull it through the stitch.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.920
Keep that working yarn around
the next gate peg, chain in the next

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.240
space, and repeat for the second space,
and then bind off the stitch.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.880
Each time before you create a chain
or bind off a stitch,

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.320
position the working yarn
around that gate peg for extra stretch.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:59.400
The bind off edge is worked
around the gate pegs.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.200
When done, pop off those loops
from the gate pegs and you'll have

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:12.160
a beautiful, stretchy edge
that accommodates the ladders that were

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.880
created by the needles out of work.

